X-WR-CALNAME:Intelligent Payroll: Czech Republic payroll deadlines
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cz-income-tax-advances@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261006T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=20
SUMMARY:Czech Republic: Withheld income tax advances on employment income (
 monthly remittance)
DESCRIPTION:The monthly remittance of the total advances withheld on employ
 ment income for a month is due on the 20th of the following month. The tax
  calendar lists a later date when the 20th falls on a weekend (for example
  22 June and 21 September 2026).\nApplies to: Employers withholding income
  tax advances\nNon-working-day rule: check the source.\n\nSource: https://
 financnisprava.gov.cz/cs/danovy-kalendar\nDetails: https://www.intelligent
 payroll.eu/deadlines.html#czech-republic\n\nFor information only\, not leg
 al or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; w
 eekends and holidays are not applied. Sources last checked 5 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#czech-republic
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cz-cssz-contributions@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261006T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=20
SUMMARY:Czech Republic: Social security contributions and monthly report to
  ČSSZ
DESCRIPTION:Employer contributions for a calendar month are payable from th
 e 1st to the 20th day of the following calendar month. Within the same per
 iod the employer submits the unified monthly report (jednotné měsíční
  hlášení) with the assessment base and contribution amount to the CSSZ.
 \nApplies to: Employers\nNon-working-day rule: check the source.\n\nSource
 : https://www.cssz.gov.cz/platba-a-terminy\nDetails: https://www.intellige
 ntpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#czech-republic\n\nFor information only\, not l
 egal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the source\;
  weekends and holidays are not applied. Sources last checked 5 October 202
 6.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#czech-republic
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cz-health-insurance-payment@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261006T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=20
SUMMARY:Czech Republic: Health insurance contributions for employees (VZP)
DESCRIPTION:Employee health insurance contributions are paid for each calen
 dar month and are payable from the 1st to the 20th day of the following ca
 lendar month.\nApplies to: Employers\nNon-working day: If the last day of 
 the payment period falls on a Saturday\, Sunday or public holiday\, the la
 st day is the nearest following working day.\nSource for non-working-day r
 ule: https://www.vzp.cz/platci/informace/zamestnavatel/splatnost-a-dalsi-z
 asady-pro-platbu-pojistneho/splatnost-pojistneho\n\nSource: https://www.vz
 p.cz/platci/informace/zamestnavatel/splatnost-a-dalsi-zasady-pro-platbu-po
 jistneho/splatnost-pojistneho\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/
 deadlines.html#czech-republic\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax a
 dvice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends and
  holidays are not applied. Sources last checked 5 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#czech-republic
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cz-health-insurance-statement@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261006T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=20
SUMMARY:Czech Republic: Statement of health insurance payments (Přehled o 
 platbách pojistného)
DESCRIPTION:Employers send each health insurer a statement of insurance pay
 ments for their insured employees no later than the 20th day of the follow
 ing month.\nApplies to: Employers\nNon-working-day rule: check the source.
 \n\nSource: https://www.vzp.cz/platci/informace/zamestnavatel/povinnosti-z
 amestnavatele/povinnost-podat-prehled-o-platbe-pojistneho\nDetails: https:
 //www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#czech-republic\n\nFor informati
 on only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated 
 by the source\; weekends and holidays are not applied. Sources last checke
 d 5 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#czech-republic
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cz-annual-withholding-settlement-electronic@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261006T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270320
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270321
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=3;BYMONTHDAY=20
SUMMARY:Czech Republic: Annual statement of withheld employment income tax 
 (vyúčtování daně)\, electronic filing
DESCRIPTION:Employers (payers of the tax) file the annual statement (vyúč
 tování) of income tax from employment withheld as advances for the previ
 ous year. Electronic filing is due by 20 March\; paper filing is due withi
 n two months after the end of the year.\nApplies to: Employers (payers of 
 the tax) withholding income tax advances on employment income\, filing ele
 ctronically\nNon-working day: If the last day of a time limit falls on a S
 aturday\, Sunday or public holiday\, the last day is the nearest following
  working day (Tax Code\, section 33(4)).\nSource for non-working-day rule:
  https://www.zakonyprolidi.cz/cs/2009-280\n\nSource: https://financnisprav
 a.gov.cz/cs/dane/dane/dan-z-prijmu/zamestnanci-zamestnavatele/dotazy-a-odp
 ovedi/2025/aktualni-dotazy-a-odpovedi-dzp-2024-a-2025\nDetails: https://ww
 w.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#czech-republic\n\nFor information o
 nly\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by t
 he source\; weekends and holidays are not applied. Sources last checked 6 
 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#czech-republic
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
